console.log('ok')\"\nThen read README.md and confirm that each exported function (this should include add, subtract, multiply and clamp) has a description of what it does, not just a bare heading.\nPASS: the script prints ok, and each exported function has a heading with a description in README.md.\nFAIL: any exported function has no heading in README.md or no description. Note that subtract was undocumented before this PR, so it must be documented now too.\n\nCheck 4. Expect line: \"npm test passes\".\nRun: npm test\nPASS: the command exits 0 and the node:test summary reports fail 0.\nFAIL: it exits non-zero or reports any failing test.\n\nAdvisory (not part of PASS/FAIL):\n- Check that test/math.test.js actually covers clamp (below, above, inside the range, and the RangeError case), and that existing tests were not deleted or weakened.\n- Check that clamp's README entry mentions the RangeError, and that add, subtract and multiply behave as before."}